LEGENDS TO VIDEO
Segment 1. The patient presented with an acute onset
of slurred speech and unsteady gait. She had evidence of
poor coordination manifested by bilateral dysmetria, dys-
diadochokinesia, and truncal ataxia.
Segment 2. The patient had a dysarthric speech.
Segment 3. The patient had a markedly increased
extensor tone in her neck and trunk, together with a
broad-based gait and extremely poor balance requiring
assistance to walk.
